  "assumptions": [
    "Conditional C-and-other-corporate payroll propensity of the group's wages equals the national propensity within industry sector and matched enterprise size.",
    "2022 SUSB propensity applies to 2024 wages.",
    "Fine industries share their broad sector legal-form propensity.",
    "NOEMP0 uses the source sector's all-size corporate payroll share, but this bin carries zero wage dollars in core.npz.",
    "Common core's frozen thin-cell pools and top-wage spread retained.",
    "Lineage added members inherit common core G3plus/white rates; ancestry-count uncertainty excluded.",
    "Government enterprise, crop/animal production, and rail cells held at the frozen key because SUSB cannot match them.",
    "SUSB excludes some funds inside merged523 and notaries inside5411: partial scope profile remains conditional.",
    "Selection_min/max remove conditional exchangeability only; retaining transported national C payroll marginals. Lineage bounds are relaxed outer envelopes rather than sharp jointly feasible bounds."
  ],
  "irs_limit": "SOI salary deductions exclude cost-of-goods-sold labor and officer compensation; officers separately shown. SOI industry is consolidated return, Census establishment. SOI excludes REIT/RIC; Census category includes other corporate forms. No payroll-level parity claimed."
}
